<title>UK: Merrill says &quot;no comment&quot; on MAM bid rumour.</title>
<headline>Merrill says &quot;no comment&quot; on MAM bid rumour.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch declined to comment on Wednesday on market speculation that it is considering a bid for Mercury Asset Management Group Plc.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't comment on market rumours,&quot; said a spokesman.</p>
<p>MAM shares rose 30p to 1,372-1/2p on the talk.</p>
<p>The group has been the subject of perennial bid speculation ever since Morgan Stanley's abortive effort to take over SG Warburg, which owned about 60 percent of MAM. MAM was eventually floated off after Swiss Bank Corp bought Warburg.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
